# Local-development defaults. NOT the configuration for any deployment.
#
# KEEP THIS FILE IDENTICAL ON `main` AND `test`.
#
# It used to differ per branch -- production hosts on main, test hosts on test -- and that is what
# broke sign-in on fhir.healthtalk.ai: merging `test` into `main` (#133) replaced main's copy with
# the test one, and the next production build shipped a bundle pointing at the test gateway. Both
# copies were valid and self-consistent, so nothing flagged it. Two identical files cannot be
# merged into the wrong one, which is why they are identical now.
#
# Deployments take their values from the Vercel project instead. For those to reach the build they
# must also be listed in turbo.json `globalEnv`: turbo runs in strict env mode and silently strips
# anything undeclared, which is how these defaults came to be the real production config in the
# first place. vite.config.ts refuses to produce a production build that resolves to any gateway
# other than authb2c.healthtalk.ai, so a repeat fails the build rather than reaching users.
MEDPLUM_BASE_URL=https://fhir-api-tst.healthtalk.ai/
MEDPLUM_CLIENT_ID=
MEDPLUM_REGISTER_ENABLED=false
MEDPLUM_GATEWAY_ENABLED=true
MEDPLUM_GATEWAY_URL=https://authb2c-tst.healthtalk.ai
MEDPLUM_GATEWAY_SERVICE_NAME=fhir-api-tst
MEDPLUM_APP_NAME=HealthTalk
